# x - y with IEEE-like results: sub_2_2, then the fix-up.
# The fix-up is that of milestone1.md, "IEEE-like results".
kernel:        sub_2_2_full
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         y = y0 y1
output:        w = w0 w1
value:         x-y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       extends w core=sub_2_2 lead=sub
min_precision: 3
source:        sub_2_2, then the fix-up of IEEE-like results (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       core: as sub_2_2; fix-up: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after an explicit test that z0 is finite (f), between the core's result and the canonical form of t; F1 to F5 of milestone1.md, "IEEE-like results", state what comes out

(z0, z1) = sub_2_2(x0, x1, y0, y1)
t        = sub(x0, y0)
a        = abs(z0)
f        = lt(a, const inf)
r0       = prod(t, const inf)
n        = eq(r0, r0)
r1       = select(n, 0, r0)
w0       = select(f, z0, r0)
w1       = select(f, z1, r1)
